### Objective
Build a Simple Student Profile using Dart.

### Requirements
* Name (**String**)
* Age (**int**)
* CGPA (**double**)
* Skills (**List<String>**)
* Subjects (**Set<String>**)
* Student Details (**Map<String, dynamic>**)
* Logged In (**bool**)
* Use **final**, **const**, **late**, and nullable variables appropriately.
* Print all values using string interpolation.

```dart
void main() {
  // final for values that won't change but might be dynamically fetched in a real app
  final String name = "Alex";
  int age = 24;
  double cgpa = 3.8;

  // const for values strictly known at compile time
  const List<String> skills = ["Dart", "Flutter", "Firebase"];
  Set<String> subjects = {"Software Engineering", "Mobile Development"};

  Map<String, dynamic> studentDetails = {
    "student_id": "STU-9921",
    "is_active": true
  };

  bool isLoggedIn = true;

  // late for variables that will definitely be initialized before use
  late String enrollmentStatus;
  enrollmentStatus = "Enrolled";

  // nullable variable for optional data
  String? graduationYear;

  print('--- Student Profile ---');
  print('Name: $name');
  print('Age: $age');
  print('CGPA:$cgpa');
  print('Skills: $skills');
  print('Subjects:$subjects');
  print('Details: $studentDetails');
  print('Logged In:$isLoggedIn');
  print('Status: $enrollmentStatus');
  print('Graduation:${graduationYear ?? "Not specified"}');
}
```
